The images were being localized. Defuddle wraps Substack images in Markdown links, so Loupe replaced the image embed but left the link’s remote URL in the note. I matched this against the extracted format for the article you tested (https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/claude-code-is-the-inflection-point).

Loupe now removes that wrapper when both URLs point to the same image, including Substack’s differently transformed CDN URLs. Links to other destinations stay intact. I mirrored the fix in the Obsidian WebP importer and documented the behavior in docs/loupe.md (/Users/josh/d/extensions/docs/loupe.md). docs/development.md is untouched.

Verification passed: 30 Loupe unit tests, 37 Obsidian importer tests, and both Loupe browser integration tests. The browser test confirms a linked image becomes a WebP asset in z-images/ with no remote URL left in the note. The full Obsidian deno task check couldn’t run because its node_modules dependencies are missing; the changed source file typechecks directly.

Reload the unpacked extension and the article tab before trying again. Images that fail to download or exceed the existing size limits will still remain remote. I also left the existing defuddle-rs/Cargo.lock modification untouched.
